    ops: persistent agent driver + model reporting + crash-guard fix (issues #4/#5)
    
    - agent-watchdog.sh: PERSISTENT driver loop (one opencode run turn per iteration,
      same session) replaces one-shot-per-cron restarts; crash-loop markers now only
      count FAILED launches so healthy steady-state relaunches never accumulate
      (kept 'agent often broken' outage from recurring); watchdog.log now logs the
      model used per turn (model=... | opencode run ...).
    - status-heartbeat.sh: report the model actually in use (parsed from the last
      '> agent · model' line of agent-run.log, fallback model.json) in current.md,
      status.log timeline and the change-signature.
    - scripts/meta-watchdog.sh (new): supervisor layer (10-min cron) — deterministic
      health checks + issue triage escalations, artifacts under status/meta/.
    - docs/05-agent-restart.md: document the persistent-loop design + model rotation.

