{"comments":[{"author":"paulzierep","body":"U should for all functional tests use the small test data, log it as always, then make a medium size benchmakr dataset once the tests work and and only after major commits run on big benchmark data","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:41:54Z"},{"author":"paulzierep","body":"Also make a plan which benchmark data to use human as host should be included so you do not excede the space limit on the drive","createdAt":"2026-09-23T17:43:46Z"},{"author":"paulzierep","body":"## Small dataset ready + both new directives addressed\n\n**Small dataset (built):** `/vol/data/datasets/comebin_small` (94 MB) — top-300 contigs by length from the demo BATS metagenome (marker-gene carrying) + all reads overlapping them via `bedtools intersect -abam … -b contigs.bed -u` (params changeable). Test runner `scripts/run_small_test.sh` writes full run bookkeeping (run_meta + command lines, comebin_run.log, resources sampler). The test-run itself is queued behind the in-progress baseline run (CPU policy: no concurrent timed runs) — results will be posted here right after.\n\n**Directive 1 — functional tests always on small data, benchmarks only after major commits:** recorded in `docs/07-fix-batches.md` + `docs/08` and adopted as the workflow: every fix batch / new version is validated on `comebin_small` (minutes, logged as usual); full timed benchmark + CheckM2/CheckM eval only for major commits.\n\n**Directive 2 — dataset \u0026 disk-space plan incl. human host-associated data:** `docs/08-dataset-space-plan.md`. Summary: 492 GB volume, **391 GB free** now; planned additions ≈ demo 6.4 + small 0.1 + CAMI II marine (1–2 samples, 10–20 GB) + **human host-associated CAMI II** (Multisample Human Microbiome Project DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518, or Toy Human Microbiome — 49 samples across 5 body sites; plan 1–2 samples ≤ 30 GB) + CAMI III (≤ 50 GB, sizes verified before download) ≈ **≤ 100 GB total → fits with \u003e50 GB headroom**. Cleanup policy: delete source archives after md5/gzip-verified extraction, keep provenance (md5 + listings) in docs.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}],"updatedAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}
{"comments":[{"author":"paulzierep","body":"## Root cause found \u0026 fixed (commit `ec41276`, pushed)\n\nThe watchdog log tells the exact story: the **17:35–18:41 UTC outage** was the crash-loop rate limiter (6 launches/6h) firing under the OLD one-shot-per-cron design — and `opencode run --auto` is a SINGLE-TURN command that exits after one assistant turn, so between restarts the agent looked 'stopped'.\n\nFixes:\n1. **Persistent driver loop** — the watchdog now launches ONE driver that keeps calling `opencode run --auto --session ses_…` turn after turn on the SAME session (context carries over) until the task is done, the agent crashes, or the 8 h / 200-turn budget is hit. flock guarantees a single driver; the next cron tick just skips while it is alive.\n2. **Crash-guard markers only count FAILED launches** — healthy steady-state relaunches never accumulate, so the rate limiter can no longer take down a working agent.\n3. **Model is now reported in the logs** — watchdog.log logs `model=\u003cid\u003e` per driver turn (incl. free-model rotation picks); `status/current.md` and `status/status.log` show the actual model in use (parsed from the transcript; currently `big-pickle`); the README banner + current.md keep a live status line every tick.\n4. **Supervisor layer** (`scripts/meta-watchdog.sh`, cron */10) monitors the watchers + GitHub issues and escalates with full transcripts pushed under `status/meta/`.\n\nCurrent: agent alive (heartbeat fresh), baseline run at epoch ~108/200. Both watchdogs + heartbeat are cron-checked every 5/10 min.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}],"updatedAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}
{"comments":[{"author":"paulzierep","body":"## Rebased on the updated fork (v1.1.0)\n\nFetched `origin/master` → `1b476a4` (Release v1.1.0 + 2 docs commits; 3251+/2515−). Assessed the changes relevant to the benchmark:\n\n- **Already upstream in v1.1.0**: `data_aug/gen_cov.py` rewritten to float64 Welford coverage means + variance (my earlier 'float coverage depth' batch-1 fix is superseded); `data_aug/gen_var.py` removed (`--addvars/--vars_sqrt` still supported); new CLI flags `-w` (Leiden workers), `-m` (HNSW neighbors), `-d` (device), `-s` (seed), `-E`, `-V`.\n- **Still broken in v1.1.0**: the bin-numbering bug (bins named by cumulative contig count; empty files for all-missing clusters) → re-applied the fix on the new base.\n\nNew branch: **`comebin-optimizations-v11`** @ `95f5ea8` (worktree `/vol/data/repos/COMEBin-v11`): sequential bin numbering + no empty/missing bins in `filter_small_bins.py` + `scripts/gen_bins_from_tsv.py`; py_compile + synthetic functional test PASS; pushed to the fork.\n\nNotes for the benchmark:\n- The in-progress baseline still runs the old snapshot (`987db95`); the README performance table now records version+commit per row so the v1.0.4-era baseline stays comparable.\n- All future runs (small-data tests, fix re-runs, CAMI II/III) switch to v1.1.0, with **`-d cpu`** (no GPU on this VM) and optionally **`-s \u003cseed\u003e`** for reproducible fix runs.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}],"updatedAt":"2026-09-23T18:56:47Z"}
